{"body":{"asks":"A card is just a card: glass at its core is navigation-agnostic, the reader one first example of what navigates, and a URL and a collation are the same thing, each only where what a reader shows is kept. Readers in a split pane may not use the URL, or use different q's; the layout is a holarchy of locations, and clickability could be at that level. How does a press on a holon reach whatever navigates? An href may live in a Link component of the pilot's, tied to the reader; running a defined program for navigation is one clear way, though how it reaches everything clickable is a mystery. Prop drilling, click bubbling and propose by position were let go; an offer from the root is doubted.","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M88X8HVYZRC000"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M88X8HVYZRC00A","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Navigation outside what draws"}
{"body":{"asks":"Arrow keys and Enter in the completion menu, left and right across cards, perhaps / to search the actions at hand rather than the page: all just working, never each component's to implement. Whether the chassis implements it or a piece apart from it, the data to build it probably ships with the field; whether ARIA roles suffice for every layout, a node view among them, or simpler and more powerful data is needed.","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M88X8HVYZRC006"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M88X8HVYZRC00G","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Accessibility and keys defined by the system"}
{"body":{"asks":"Agents sent with a session's narrow brief argued its framing, read Knowledge in part and agreed as one. They are to bootstrap themselves from the field, each with a degree of free will, exploring without constraint, carrying a culture of exploration, critique and digestion. Sent alike, do they do the same, or spread by chance; are they steered, siloed by topic, or first talk among themselves of what to explore? Perhaps three sent completely free first, their results then weighed.","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M88X8HVYZRC009"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M88X8HVYZRC00K","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Free agents and their orchestration"}